# tests/ — message-log tests

- `098-run-tests [DIR]` — runs 091–094 against the stand-in room-folders
  and, if present, the real one; exits non-zero on any failure.
- `090-test-harness.lua` — `start(arg, name)` → harness with `rooms`, `log`,
  `fresh_home(settings table)` → home, `new_room(home)` → room id,
  `message(fields)` → message with a fresh id, `settings(shape, mixing,
  check, edits)` → config table, `check(bool, label)`, `refuses(fn,
  expected_text, label)`, `finish()` (prints counts, exits 1 on failure).
  Scratch homes go in `tmp/shared-memory/message-log/<test>-<neighbour>/`.
- `091-test-codecs.lua` — round trips of 229 texts per shape, markers, damaged records.
- `092-test-log.lua` — filing, duplicates, order, bell, copy, refusals, for all 12 setting combinations.
- `093-test-edits.lua` — never / corrections / window in every shape.
- `094-test-mixing-and-memory.lua` — shape changes under fixed and per-record; remembered check vs outside appends and replaced files.
- `095-measure.lua [DIR] [real|stand-in] [count]` — bytes per message and timings.
- `stand-in/002-room-folders.lua` — a small copy of 101's functions used by the log, for testing alone.

Each test file is run as `luajit <file> [DIR] [real|stand-in]`.
